<document ids="differences-to-the-html4css1-writer" names="differences\ to\ the\ html4css1\ writer" source="html5-features.rst" title="Differences to the html4css1 Writer"><title>Differences to the <title_reference>html4css1</title_reference> Writer</title><bullet_list bullet="*"><list_item><paragraph>Use only <problematic ids="problematic-1" refid="system-message-1">meta_</problematic> keywords recognized by HTML 5.
Add HTML5-compatible meta tags for docinfo items
"authors", "date", and "copyright".</paragraph><paragraph>Add a <reference anonymous="1" name="viewport meta tag" refuri="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Viewport_meta_tag">viewport meta tag</reference> to tell mobile browsers
to use the device-width as viewport.</paragraph><target anonymous="1" ids="target-1" refuri="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Viewport_meta_tag"></target></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Set table column widths with &lt;style="width: ..."&gt;, not "width" argument.</paragraph></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Horizontal alignment of table heads with CSS.</paragraph></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Do not drop paragraph elements, use CSS rules to prevent unwanted vertical
space.</paragraph></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Put subtitles in &lt;p&gt; elements.</paragraph></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Use the new semantic tags &lt;main&gt;, &lt;section&gt;, &lt;header&gt;,
&lt;footer&gt;, &lt;aside&gt;, &lt;figure&gt;, and &lt;figcaption&gt;.
See <literal>minimal.css</literal> and <literal>responsive.css</literal> for styling rule examples.</paragraph><paragraph>Change the <title_reference>initial_header_level</title_reference> setting default to "2", as browsers
use the <reference anonymous="1" name="same style for &lt;h1&gt; and &lt;h2&gt; when nested in a &lt;section&gt;" refuri="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/39547412/same-font-size-for-h1-and-h2-in-article">same style for &lt;h1&gt; and &lt;h2&gt; when nested in a &lt;section&gt;</reference>.</paragraph><target anonymous="1" ids="target-2" refuri="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/39547412/same-font-size-for-h1-and-h2-in-article"></target></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Use HTML5 tags &lt;small&gt;, &lt;s&gt;, &lt;q&gt;, &lt;dfn&gt;, &lt;var&gt;, &lt;samp&gt;, &lt;kbd&gt;,
&lt;i&gt;, &lt;b&gt;, &lt;u&gt;, &lt;mark&gt;, and &lt;bdi&gt; if a matching class value
is found in <title_reference>inline</title_reference> and <title_reference>literal</title_reference> elements.
Use &lt;ins&gt; and &lt;del&gt; if a matching class value
is found in <title_reference>inline</title_reference>, <title_reference>literal</title_reference>, or <title_reference>container</title_reference> elements.
(See <problematic ids="problematic-2" refid="system-message-2">`text-level semantics`_</problematic> and <problematic ids="problematic-3" refid="system-message-3">`indicating edits`_</problematic>.)</paragraph></list_item><list_item><paragraph>Use &lt;img&gt; tags for SVG images and &lt;video&gt; for video formats.</paragraph></list_item><list_item><image align="right" alt="blue square" loading="embed" uri="../input/data/blue%20square.png"></image><paragraph>Embed images or defer fetching images with the <reference name="image-loading" refuri="https://docutils.sourceforge.io/docs/user/config.html#image-loading">image-loading</reference>
configuration setting or the "loading" option of the "image" directive.</paragraph><image align="right" height="16" loading="lazy" uri="../../../docs/user/rst/images/biohazard.png" width="16"></image><paragraph>Especially with "lazy" loading, it is strongly recommended to
specify both width and height of the image to prevent content layout
shifts or use the "scale" option to let the writer insert the size
determined from the image file.</paragraph></list_item></bullet_list><target ids="image-loading" names="image-loading" refuri="https://docutils.sourceforge.io/docs/user/config.html#image-loading"></target><section ids="field-list-rendering" names="field\ list\ rendering"><title>Field List Rendering</title><paragraph>A <title_reference>field list</title_reference> is converted to a HTML <title_reference>definition list</title_reference> and given the
